+# BUG-260801-1iu1ln solution-architecture handoff
+
+## Outcome
+
+Keep **BUG-260801-1iu1ln — bind-rc6-lifecycle-to-observed-csk-traces** as the single development unit. No child or sibling task is added: the board hierarchy makes this Bug a leaf, and the remaining cycle-10 publication-observer defect is one cohesive deliverable inside the Bug's existing lifecycle-binding ownership. A separate item would duplicate its acceptance boundary and downstream blocker.
+
+## Requirement traceability
+
+| Remaining developer work | Concrete requirement |
+| --- | --- |
+| Retain captured native-loader `os.utime` mutate/restore regression on POSIX and a Windows-equivalent regression or explicit fail-closed platform classification | Acceptance Criteria: every normative field is checked against observed trace/state; cycle-10 reviewer required rework 1 |
+| Classify relevant supported post-handoff content, metadata, ownership, timestamp, xattr/flags and namespace mutations; ensure the complete publication case differs for each | Acceptance Criteria: all lifecycle cases drive CocoaSkills seams and every normative field is observed; cycle-10 reviewer required rework 2 |
+| Make audit-hook mutation classification exhaustive and fail closed on newly relevant unclassified events | Scope: exhaustive scalar-leaf mutation coverage or fail-closed normative-field classification; cycle-10 reviewer required rework 3 |
+| Run native barrier, inherited sabotage, exact-root canonical/scalar/classification, full authenticated conformance, strict mypy, diff/provenance, packaging/release guards and relevant Windows lane | Acceptance Criteria: focused exact-root tests, strict mypy and diff checks pass; cycle-10 reviewer required rework 4 |
+| Preserve exact signed base, release exclusions, signed commit evidence, task outcome and CocoaSkills logbook entry | Scope and Acceptance Criteria: exact ba250bf base, signed integration commit, no pin/schema-v7/tag/release/claim change; cycle-10 reviewer required rework 5 |
+
+## Gap and scope audit
+
+Sections checked: Description, Scope, Acceptance Criteria, cycle-10 reviewer verdict, explicit release-surface exclusions, and current dependency edge to TASK-260720-12r55p.
+
+Result: no beyond-literal-spec element is justified. The newly explicit mutation-class checklist is a refinement of the existing observed-state and fail-closed requirements, not new product scope. No research task is justified because the reviewer verdict answers the open implementation boundary. No diagram materially improves this one-boundary repair.
+
+## Dependencies and execution
+
+The Bug is unblocked and remains the sole implementation pickup. Its existing `blocks TASK-260720-12r55p` edge correctly prevents shared-v6-vector consumption until review accepts the lifecycle binding. No dependency changes are required.
+
+The five newly added checklist items are the development-ready remaining work and local verification gates.

